# LF in the working tree on every machine, not just in the index.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and built by CI on macOS and Linux. Without
# this, files sit permanently "modified" with an EMPTY diff on the Windows
# checkout, which is how the sibling yarg-song-server repo ended up stamping
# `vcs.modified=true` into every binary it built - a difference that looks like a
# toolchain problem and is not one. Same trap here: Capacitor hashes the web
# assets it copies into the native projects, so a CRLF checkout and an LF one
# produce different `dist/` bytes from one commit.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect genuinely binary content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Native project scaffolding, once `cap add` has written it, contains Xcode and
# Gradle files that tooling rewrites; they are gitignored, but if that ever
# changes they are not ours to normalise.
ios/** -text
android/** -text
